From: queuetruth contributors
Subject: [PATCH] PartialFillExchange: remove orders that a maker fill completes (#312)

A queue-position fill that leaves less than half a lot makes `fill()` mark the order
`Filled`, but `check_if_buy_filled` / `check_if_sell_filled` registered the order for
removal only when the fill was strictly larger than the leaves. The completed order
stayed in the book, and the next trade at or through its price called `fill()` on it
again: `BacktestError::InvalidOrderStatus`, `elapse` returns 14 and the backtest stops.

Register the order for removal whenever the leaves left after the execution round to
zero lots, the same rule `fill()` uses for the status. This covers
`filled_qty == leaves_qty` and a sub-lot floating-point residual (lot 0.01, qty 0.1:
leaves 0.09000000000000001 after a one-lot fill, queue fill 0.09), which a `>`
-> `>=` change alone does not. Executed quantities are unchanged.

Tests: 7 Rust unit tests in partialfillexchange.rs (5 fail before the fix, 2 guard
existing behaviour) and 5 Python tests in py-hftbacktest/tests (4 fail on 2.4.4).

Fixes #312.
---
